fix: load the profile data at mount instead of staging it behind scroll

The snapshots ARE the content of the middle of the site, but they were only
requested once scroll progress crossed a threshold — which made the copy
hostage to the render loop. Any stall in the frame loop and the chapters sit
at zero, which reads as broken rather than as loading, and the count-up then
animates from a placeholder that was never real.

All three sources now load when the experience mounts. ~126KB of JSON is a
cheap price for content that is guaranteed to be there when its chapter
arrives, and it removes an entire class of timing bug along with the staging
plumbing that carried it.
